SALESFORCE

Salesforce Mini Project – Step-by-Step Guide (Very Simple)
You can make a simple Student Management System or Employee Management System in Salesforce. This is enough for practical exams and viva.

What You Will Build
A custom Salesforce app with:
* Custom Object
* Fields
* Tabs
* Records
* Reports
Example Project: Student Management System

STEP 1 — Create Salesforce Free Account
Go to:
Salesforce Developer Signup
Fill:
* Name
* Email
* Username → use unique email
* Country
Click Sign Me Up
Then:
* Verify email
* Set password
Login at:
Salesforce Login

STEP 2 — Open Setup
After login:
1. Click ⚙️ Gear icon (top right)
2. Click Setup

STEP 3 — Create Custom App
Search:
App Manager
Then:
1. Click App Manager
2. Click New Lightning App
Fill:
Field	Value
App Name	Student Management
Description	Mini Project
Click:
* Next
* Next
* Save & Finish

STEP 4 — Create Custom Object
Search:
Object Manager
Then:
1. Click Create
2. Click Custom Object
Fill:
Field	Value
Label	Student
Plural Label	Students
Record Name	Student Name
Tick:
* Allow Reports
* Launch New Tab Wizard
Click:
Save

STEP 5 — Create Fields
Inside Student Object:
Go:
Fields & Relationships → New
Create these fields:
Field Type	Field Name
Number	Roll Number
Email	Email
Phone	Phone
Date	Admission Date
Picklist	Course
For Course values:
BCA
BBA
MCA
MBA
Click Save after each.

STEP 6 — Create Tab
After saving object:
1. Tab Style → choose any color/icon
2. Next
3. Save

STEP 7 — Add Object to App
Go:
App Manager
1. Edit your app
2. Navigation Items
3. Add:
    * Students
Save.

STEP 8 — Run the Application
Now:
1. Click App Launcher (9 dots)
2. Open:
Student Management
You will see:
* Students Tab
Click:
New
Add sample data.
Example:
Name	Roll No	Course
Arpit	101	MCA
Save.

STEP 9 — Create Report
Search:
Reports
Then:
1. New Report
2. Select:
Students
1. Create Report
You can show:
* Student Names
* Courses
* Emails
Save Report.

STEP 10 — Create Dashboard (Optional)
Search:
Dashboards
1. New Dashboard
2. Add chart
3. Use Student Report
Save.

HOW TO RUN DURING PRACTICAL
Quick Demo Flow
1. Login Salesforce
2. Open Student Management App
3. Open Students Tab
4. Click New
5. Add Student Record
6. Show Reports
Done ✅
